  "name": "Bench-Anchored Supine Trunk Hold",
  "definition": "A bilateral isometric core family performed seated at the edge of a bench with the lower body held in place by a partner. The athlete reclines the straight trunk to about 45 degrees relative to the bench and holds without spinal or hip motion. Gravity tends to extend the spine and hips; those are resisted tendencies rather than dynamic repetitions. This contract covers the exact 45-degree training hold, not the separately described 60-degree assessment, unsupported hollow holds, sit-ups, or partner perturbations.",
